{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'git diff --no-ext-diff -- docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml docs/test/test-cases.toml; git status --short -- docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml docs/test/test-cases.toml'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\nindex d6eed5139..e642d8f41 100644\n--- a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n+++ b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n@@ -1561,7 +1561,7 @@ sr_refs = [\"SR-157\"]\n title = \"Test-file declarations of their test cases\"\n module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/gen_arch_map.py;project-trajectory/scripts/trajectory_arch.py\"\n code_symbol = \"read_test_tags/tc_tag_findings\"\n-detail = \"A test-file back-link declaration names test cases, and each named id must be a live test case. In a Python test file, declarations in the module docstring and in a test's docstring are read; in another supported test-file type, declarations are read at file level. A byte-order mark at the start of a file does not change its reading. The two Python levels union. A test repeating its module's test case is no finding. A non-docstring string literal, a backtick-quoted token and an unsupported test-file type make no declaration. A declaration outside a read position, including a pytest-fixture docstring, is refused as misplaced. The following are refused as malformed: a declaration whose list is not test-case ids only; a read-position line whose token follows prose and names a test case; and a next line that continues a valid list. The after-prose refusal directs the declaration to the start of its own line. An id absent from the live test-case registry, including an example or retired id, is refused as unknown; a Drafted test case is live. A test file that cannot be decoded or parsed is refused as unreadable. Every live id in a valid declaration maps to its test node. Each refusal names the repository-relative file, line and shape. Reading test files does not change source-file declaration reading. An absent tests root, or an absent test-case registry, makes the check vacuous. Findings warn without strict checking and error under strict checking; they gate from DevStg-Impl and remain warnings below that rung, including in a newly created project. The contract covers test files, test-case registries and declared tests roots produced by supported workflows; non-Python fixture text, non-default test-collection patterns, hand-chosen test-case aliases and tests roots reached through a symlink are outside it.\"\n+detail = \"A test-file back-link declaration names test cases, and each named id must be a live test case. In a Python test file, declarations in the module docstring and in a test's docstring are read; in another supported test-file type, declarations are read at file level. A byte-order mark at the start of a file does not change its reading. The two Python levels union. A test repeating its module's test case is no finding. That reading judges the declarations alone: their equality with the Evidence cell is a separate rule. A non-docstring string literal, a backtick-quoted token and an unsupported test-file type make no declaration. A declaration outside a read position, including a pytest-fixture docstring, is refused as misplaced. The following are refused as malformed: a declaration whose list is not test-case ids only; a read-position line whose token follows prose and names a test case; and a next line that continues a valid list. The after-prose refusal directs the declaration to the start of its own line. An id absent from the live test-case registry, including an example or retired id, is refused as unknown; a Drafted test case is live. A test file that cannot be decoded or parsed is refused as unreadable. Every live id in a valid declaration maps